{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "def fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The FibFib number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fibfib(0) == 0\n    fibfib(1) == 0\n    fibfib(2) == 1\n    fibfib(n) == fibfib(n-1) + fibfib(n-2) + fibfib(n-3).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fibfib number sequence.\n    >>> fibfib(1)\n    0\n    >>> fibfib(5)\n    4\n    >>> fibfib(8)\n    24\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a, b, c to fibfib(0), fibfib(1), fibfib(2) respectively.\n    a, b, c = 0, 0, 1\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next fibfib number using the recurrence relation.\n        next_fibfib = a + b + c\n        # Shift the window for the next iteration.\n        a, b, c = b, c, next_fibfib\n    return c"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x, shift):\n    x_str = str(x)\n    n = len(x_str)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    if shift > n:\n        return x_str[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Perform circular shift\n        effective_shift = shift % n\n        if effective_shift == 0:\n            return x_str\n        \n        # Split and concatenate for right circular shift\n        right_part = x_str[n - effective_shift:]\n        left_part = x_str[:n - effective_shift]\n        return right_part + left_part"}
